# Machin-like formulas for the logarithms of the first n primes and for the
# irreducible angles of the first n nonreal Gaussian primes, as found by
# machin_set (https://github.com/fredrik-johansson/machin).
#
#   atanh_<n>_P = [p_1, ..., p_n]              (the first n primes)
#   log(p_i) = (1/den) * sum_j C[i][j] * atanh(1/X[j])
#
#   atan_<n>_P = [(a_1, b_1), ..., (a_n, b_n)] (Gaussian primes a + b*i, ordered
#                by norm, first 1 + i, then the representative with 0 < a < b)
#   atan(b_i/a_i) = (1/den) * sum_j C[i][j] * atan(1/X[j])
#
#   <name>_mu = sum_j 1/log10(X[j])            (Lehmer's measure)
#
# All formulas are optimal among n-term formulas with X[j] < 2^126 (see the
# README), except n = 40 and n = 48, which come from a heuristic search.
# The file is valid Python; check_machin_formulas.py verifies it.

